	(text "PCjr Signaling\nTechnical Reference 2-29 I/O Channel I/O Map Table\n  - 98 7654 3210\n  - 00 1111 Xaaa - Port 0F8-0FF (Diskette) [For Reference]\n  - 10 1111 1aaa - Port 2F8-2FF (Serial Port) [For Reference]\n  - 11 1111 1aaa - Port 3F8-3FF (Modem)\nTechnical Reference 3-70 Internal Modem\n  - IRQ4 (Positive-Active)\nTechnical Reference 3-72 Internal Modem\n~{MODEM_CS}/~{DISKETTE_CS} is asserted low for both Modem & Diskette access\nA9 - Used in conjunction with ~{MODEM_CS}/~{DISKETTE_CS} to select which device\n~{A9} + ~{MODEM_CS}/~{DISKETTE_CS} = Port 0F8-0FF = Diskette  [For Reference]\nA9 + ~{MODEM_CS}/~{DISKETTE_CS} = Port 3F8-3FF = Modem\nTechnical Reference 3-73 Internal Modem\n~{IOR} = Read when used with A9 + ~{MODEM_CS}\n~{IOW} = Write when used with A9 + ~{MODEM_CS}\n~{CART_INSTALL} = Card should assert if it has an 8250 UART, should NOT assert if it doesn't\n  - jrNIC is not an 8250 UART, so does *not* assert"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -16.002 -105.791 0)
		(effects
